# D-PEER-OPEN-UNLINKED-CHAIN-REMOVE-FAILS-IFREE-SHUTDOWN-BOTH-NODES: step (1)
# of the record, reproduce on build X (main tree ~/src/mxfs, srcversion
# C06A6D4A9AB7A357503DF51, 0.90.131) with no test knob, keeping the LUN image
# after a failure.  The record's two laps (cmwd1, cmwn1) ran build F
# (4533348C8D27CA5288B31CA, build X plus the read-only dbg_clmerge_recheck
# check, on in both laps); this queue runs the same workload
# (tests/clmerge_window_node.sh) on build X with every knob at its default.
# The harness refuses a node running anything else.
#
# The laps: two with the module's `instr` parameter at its default 0, then one
# with instr=1 (P83-UNL-REMCHK logs every remove's in-core next against the
# platter's, for hypothesis H-U2; it adds a FUA dinode read per remove).  All on
# 2/net/mesh/direct g2c, where both failures were seen, 30 iterations each.
#
# HYPOTHESES (the record's, written before any patch):
#   H-U1, the NOPREV arm: the remove of z needs its predecessor y in core, and
#     nothing keeps y in core on the owner once the peer is y's last closer; the
#     predecessor preflight runs only when z's own chain state is incomplete.
#   H-U2, the BACKREF arm: an in-core i_next_unlinked of a chain member is not
#     refreshed when a peer's free of that member's successor rewrites its
#     di_next_unlinked on the platter.
#
# VERDICT RULES (written before the first lap):
#   REPRODUCED  any lap REPRODUCED: the defect is on build X with no knob.  Its
#               kept image and both nodes' traces decide which arm it was:
#               H-U1 SUPPORTED for a NOPREV whose prev is on the image's bucket
#               chain with nlink 0 and whose in-core copy on that node was
#               reclaimed (P140-RECLAIM-COMMIT) before the failure with no
#               reload after it; H-U2 SUPPORTED for a BACKREF whose next is free
#               on the image while the image's chain does not name it there, or
#               a P83-UNL-REMCHK STALE=1 line for the freed inode before the
#               failure (instr lap); PLATTER-INCONSISTENT when the image's own
#               chain names a free inode, which is an integrity defect in its
#               own right and is recorded as one.
#   PASS        all three laps PASS: the shape did not recur on build X in 90
#               iterations.  That disposes of nothing; the next step is an arm
#               that forces the window (y reclaimed on the owner before z's
#               inactivation), written as its own hypothesis first.
#   VACUOUS     a lap whose owner completed no acknowledged iteration measured
#               nothing; the workload is redesigned before any claim.
#   FAIL        no remove failed and no node failed, but the workload or the
#               cold audit did: attributed before anything else.
#
# Bound per lap (tests/peer_open_unlinked_chain.sh's derivation): prep 300 +
# srcversion and the instr knob 2x20 + 2x20 + mkdir 30 + workload 30 x (3 + 5
# + ceil(3 x 0.3) + 2) + 60 = 390, +10 for the peer + the owner's done fallback
# 20 + instr reset 2x20 + stream copy 2x120 + on a failure: unmount 2x(70 + 20)
# + snapshot 60 (the final-verification queues' term) + image check 10, + the
# cold audit 150 = 1515 s.
1515 MXFS_SNAPSHOT_DIR=/mxfs/snapshots PUC_INSTR=0 tests/peer_open_unlinked_chain.sh puca1 30 2/net/mesh/direct g2c
1515 MXFS_SNAPSHOT_DIR=/mxfs/snapshots PUC_INSTR=0 tests/peer_open_unlinked_chain.sh puca2 30 2/net/mesh/direct g2c
1515 MXFS_SNAPSHOT_DIR=/mxfs/snapshots PUC_INSTR=1 tests/peer_open_unlinked_chain.sh puci1 30 2/net/mesh/direct g2c
